		{
			"id": "112321721791727175",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer/112321721775053110",
			"author": {
				"name": "Alan Norbauer",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-04-23T17:30:59.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> It doesn’t support exporting optimized/minified images but it does have an image component that will export your images.</p><p>A silly limitation, and your point on incentives is obviously still valid, but it is much less silly than fully not supporting images.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112321747708138181",
			"parentId": "112321721791727175",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/112321747708138181",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-04-23T17:37:35.409Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>alannorbauer</span></a></span> by “export” do you mean that it will swap to use a static image url as-is without changing your &lt;Image&gt; app code or paths to the image?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112321814640044149",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer/112321814626243113",
			"author": {
				"name": "Alan Norbauer",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-04-23T17:54:36.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Yeah. I have a layer of indirection on my site, but this markdown: <a href=\"https://github.com/altano/alan.norbauer.com/blob/b252e36306ca39747583b73952943508c45526a0/src/content/articles/disable-source-maps/index.mdx?plain=1#L30\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">github.com/altano/alan.norbaue</span><span class=\"invisible\">r.com/blob/b252e36306ca39747583b73952943508c45526a0/src/content/articles/disable-source-maps/index.mdx?plain=1#L30</span></a></p><p>Goes into this Image component: <a href=\"https://github.com/altano/alan.norbauer.com/blob/b252e36306ca39747583b73952943508c45526a0/mdx-components.tsx#L61\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">github.com/altano/alan.norbaue</span><span class=\"invisible\">r.com/blob/b252e36306ca39747583b73952943508c45526a0/mdx-components.tsx#L61</span></a></p><p>Which produces:</p><p>```html<br>&lt;img alt=\"…\" … srcSet=\"/_next/image?…\" src=\"/_next/image?…\"/&gt;<br>```</p><p>And I can turn export on/off without changing the Image component usage. The only thing that has to be toggled on/off to export is image optimization.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112321965528799916",
			"parentId": "112321814640044149",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/112321965528799916",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-04-23T18:32:59.090Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>alannorbauer</span></a></span> not sure I understand what you mean. When you static export your site, whether or not you use `&lt;Image&gt;` or `&lt;img&gt;` in your markdown—it produces `&lt;img src=&quot;/_next/image?…&quot;&gt;`?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112321981785222121",
			"parentId": "112321965528799916",
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer/112321981723510148",
			"author": {
				"name": "Alan Norbauer",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-04-23T18:37:06.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Sorry, the markdown muddied the waters. I have it configured so that markdown images go through the next Image component, whether I use an &lt;img/&gt; tag or a markdown image, but that isn’t necessary.</p><p>If you take the Markdown out of the equation, I’m just saying you can use the Image component and it will work, whether you export or serve dynamically. And the only change you need to make to your app code is turning off image optimization.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112322009086113088",
			"parentId": "112321981785222121",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/112322009086113088",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-04-23T18:44:03.722Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>alannorbauer</span></a></span> ah, I’m getting closer! So when image optimization is turned off (in this example)—what markup is produced?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
