			},
			"date": "2024-04-23T18:57:00.987Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>alannorbauer</span></a></span> ah this is why I’m confused! In this example it’s still running the static image through the next image service, is it not?</p><p>e.g.: &lt;img alt=&quot;Screenshot of the Firefox debugger with source maps off&quot; src=&quot;/_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fsource-map-example-tooltip-off.0d067dde.png&amp;amp;w=3840&amp;amp;q=75&quot;/&gt;</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112322184452891854",
			"parentId": "112322060025000580",
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer/112322184440814566",
			"author": {
				"name": "Alan Norbauer",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-04-23T19:28:39.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Well, I believe I was mistaken. When I export I can see the exported image file but it isn’t used. The Image component points at an image service. A test with `npx http-server out` shows my images don’t load. I don’t know what I was thinking suggesting that _anything_ in Next worked.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112322194854970145",
			"parentId": "112322184452891854",
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer/112322194838994169",
			"author": {
				"name": "Alan Norbauer",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@alannorbauer",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-04-23T19:31:18.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> This is actually why I was worried when Astro started supporting dynamic sites. I thought they were going to lose focus on the SSG side of things, but so far that hasn’t happened. (I’m one PR away from happily switching to Astro - <a href=\"https://github.com/withastro/astro/compare/main...altano:astro:image-middleware\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">github.com/withastro/astro/com</span><span class=\"invisible\">pare/main...altano:astro:image-middleware</span></a>)</p>",
