		{
			"id": "112325332286241832",
			"parentId": "112321014154560471",
			"url": "https://mstdn.jp/@otowa0/112325332264633624",
			"author": {
				"name": "Otowa",
				"url": "https://mstdn.jp/@otowa0",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/112/211/735/835/430/957/original/18223ebda59741ab.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-04-24T08:49:11.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> React officially recommends using frameworks, and it feels like a problem when considering that NextJS is mentioned first. If it says on the first page of the documentation, \"Do you want to use the most popular framework? ① Pay $20 a month to Vercel...,\" will everyone use React?</p>",
